title: July 2027

@sikorski_p2050_refugees_2027
# prose-audit: Grade A — The third wave stays a wing rather than a party and Razem's objection is the right one. Social floor, state-capacity bureau and public congress differ in what the enlarged Left becomes, including a bureau built to tell its own ministers that a promise is undeliverable.
title: Poland 2050's social wing seeks shelter in [+ left_party_name +]
subtitle: State-capacity reformers and green centrists refuse to remain the softer face of the Konfederacja compact
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 55
order: 1
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2027 and month = 7 and sikorski_nightmare = 1 and sikorski_refugee_wave = 2 and p2050_seats > 0 and p2050_joined_left = 0
on-arrival: {!
const p2050SeatsBefore = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.round(Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0)
);
const p2050SocialShare = Math.min(
    0.55,
    0.30 +
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.p2050_state_capacity_share) || 0) - 40) / 200 +
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.sikorski_protest_strength) || 0) - 30) / 400
);
const p2050Transfer = Math.min(
    p2050SeatsBefore,
    Math.max(1, Math.round(p2050SeatsBefore * p2050SocialShare))
);
Q.p2050_social_joined_left = 1;
Q.left_p2050_current_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_p2050_current_seats) || 0) +
    p2050Transfer;
Q.p2050_seats = Math.max(0, p2050SeatsBefore - p2050Transfer);
Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) + p2050Transfer;
Q.left_progressives_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0) +
    p2050Transfer;
Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - p2050Transfer
);
Q.sikorski_refugee_seats += p2050Transfer;
Q.sikorski_refugee_wave = 3;
Q.sikorski_minority_government =
    Q.government_support_seats < 231 ? 1 : 0;
Q.sikorski_government_status = Q.sikorski_minority_government
    ? "Minority government awaiting the election under opposition toleration"
    : "Nominal majority held together after three refugee waves";
Q.coalition_status = Q.sikorski_government_status;
Q.p2050_state_capacity_share = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.p2050_state_capacity_share) || 0) - 18
);
Q.p2050_coalition_dissent += 30;
Q.progressives_strength += 5;
Q.party_unity += 2;
Q.razem_dissent += 6;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 4;
if ((Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0) <= 0) {
    Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet = 0;
}
Q.news_headline = p2050Transfer +
    " Poland 2050 social-reform MPs enter " + Q.left_party_name;
!}

= July 2027 — A shelter becomes a new internal map

**[+ left_p2050_current_seats +] Poland 2050 deputies** from the
state-capacity, green-centrist and social-reform wing leave the government
camp. They enter **[+ left_party_name +]** as a Poland 2050 current rather than
claiming that the whole centrist party has merged. The remaining party keeps
its name, seats and market-liberal and Christian-democratic wings.

Three waves now sit under one roof: Trzaskowski's civic network, iPL and the
Greens, and the social reformers from Poland 2050. Together they have moved
**[+ sikorski_refugee_seats +] MPs** from Sikorski's side of the chamber to
ours. **[+ sikorski_government_status +].**

Razem warns that "social reformer" is not yet a socialist programme. It wants
the newcomers bound to public housing, progressive taxation, stronger unions
and services provided outside the market before they receive list guarantees.

- @sikorski_p2050_social_floor_2027
- @sikorski_p2050_capacity_2027
- @sikorski_p2050_congress_2027

@sikorski_p2050_social_floor_2027
title: Make the common social floor permanent
subtitle: Require every refugee current to defend labour enforcement, equality and public services.
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 4; progressive_credibility += 4; party_unity += 4; razem_dissent -= 4; razem_cooperation += 3; coalition_blur -= 4; news_headline = "The refugee currents accept one permanent Left social floor"

The floor is written before the places are allocated: labour enforcement,
public provision and the enacted equality laws, binding on every current
including the ones that arrived last month. Nobody negotiates a list place
until they have signed it.

Razem, which has spent three years demanding exactly this document, gets it
from an unexpected direction and says so with some grace. The state-capacity
reformers sign because the alternative is Sikorski, which is not much of a
choice and is still theirs to make.

- @poland_event_queue: Write the floor first

@sikorski_p2050_capacity_2027
title: Give Poland 2050's reformers a state-capacity bureau
subtitle: Preserve their administrative expertise without restoring a centrist veto over the programme.
on-arrival: administrative_capacity += 5; government_delivery += 2; progressives_dissent += 2; barons_dissent += 2; razem_dissent += 2; razem_cooperation -= 1; news_headline = "The Poland 2050 refugees build a state-capacity bureau inside the Left"

The reformers get a bureau: budget analysis, delivery planning and the
unglamorous machinery of making a ministry work, staffed by people who have
actually run one. It is a genuine asset and the Left has never had one.

It is also a centre of expertise that can tell any future Lewica minister that
a promise is undeliverable. That is what it is for, and the first time it does
it the party will have to decide whether it wanted advice or agreement.

- @poland_event_queue: Stand up the bureau

@sikorski_p2050_congress_2027
title: Call a refugee-currents congress before the election
subtitle: Let old and new currents renegotiate lists, leadership and identity in public.
on-arrival: party_unity += 2; public_trust += 3; media_capacity += 3; organiser_energy -= 2; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 9; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 8; news_headline = "The enlarged Left calls a congress of old and refugee currents"

Everything is settled in public: lists, leadership, programme, the standing of
each current, argued out at a congress with press in the hall six weeks before
a national campaign.

It is either the bravest or the most reckless decision of the year, and the
distinction will not be available until the votes are counted. What it produces
is a party whose internal settlement nobody can later claim was imposed —
assembled at maximum volume, in front of everybody, on the worst possible
schedule.

- @poland_event_queue: Call the congress
